# Top-level development / CI toolchain for taintly.
#
# taintly ships ZERO runtime dependencies; everything here is dev/build
# tooling used only in CI. This file lists the DIRECT pins; the fully
# resolved, hash-pinned lock lives in requirements-dev.lock and is what
# CI installs under `pip install --require-hashes`.
#
# Regenerate the lock after any change here:
#
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes \
#     --python-version 3.10 -o requirements-dev.lock requirements-dev.in
#
# `--universal` resolves across platforms and Python versions; the
# explicit `--python-version 3.10` sets the lower bound to the oldest
# interpreter CI runs so the single lock carries marker-gated transitive
# deps (tomli, exceptiongroup for <3.11; colorama for win32) for the
# whole 3.10 / 3.11 / 3.12 matrix. Omitting it would default the floor
# to the host interpreter and silently drop the 3.10-only entries,
# breaking `pip install --require-hashes` on the 3.10 matrix leg. Keep
# the direct pins below in lockstep with the versions cited in
# .github/workflows/ comments.

ruff==0.15.16
mypy==2.1.0
hypothesis==6.165.10
bandit==1.9.4
pip==26.2
pip-audit==2.10.0
pytest
pytest-timeout
pytest-cov
pytest-xdist
